  {
    "id": "8e7552c69f373b5b",
    "title": "Saviynt Brings AI Identity Security to Global Stage With UNLOCK 2026 Roadshow",
    "summary": "Saviynt, a leading provider of identity security solutions, today announced its global UNLOCK 2026 Roadshow. It will explore a new era of identity security where the focus moves beyond managing access to securing intelligence. Throughout the 12-city series, Saviynt will convene security executives, identity practitioners, customers, partners, and industry experts to examine how organisations can secure every human, non-human, and AI identity and make identity a strategic advantage in the age of AI.\nAs AI takes on a greater role across the enterprise, identity security is becoming critical to its safe adoption. Recent industry research found that 70% of organisations say AI systems have more access than a human in the same role would receive, highlighting the growing challenge of governing AI identities and enforcing appropriate access controls. To help organisations address these challenges, Saviynt recently launched Zuma, its complete AI identity security platform. During UNLOCK, attendees will explore practical strategies for securing AI-powered operations, governing human, non-human, and AI identities, and modernising identity security to reduce risk while accelerating innovation. \nDiscover the future of AI identity security through visionary keynotes and product innovations\nHear real-world customer success stories showcasing how organisations are securing all identities while accelerating digital transformation\nGain strategic insights from industry leaders on securing AI agents, modernising identity programs, and preparing for the next generation of enterprise security\nExperience live demonstrations of Saviynt's AI-powered identity platform and intelligent automation capabilities\nConnect with peers and experts through executive roundtables, networking sessions, and one-on-one discussions with Saviynt leadership and identity security specialists\n\"AI is fundamentally changing who or what needs access inside the enterprise,\" said Sachin Nayyar, Founder and CEO of Saviynt. \"This is a defining moment for identity security. Following the launch of Zuma, we have seen firsthand how rapidly organisations are rethinking identity in the age of AI, both as an Agentic Identity Platform and Identity Security for AI. UNLOCK gives us an opportunity to hear directly from the enterprises navigating this change, and those conversations will continue to inspire how we innovate and help our customers securely unlock AI's full potential.\"\nAmazon Web Services (AWS) is the global sponsor of Saviynt UNLOCK 2026, supporting conversations on how organisations can securely adopt and scale AI while strengthening security, governance, and trust.\nThe UNLOCK 2026 Roadshow will visit the following cities:\nLondon, September 15\nFrankfurt, September 17\nHaarlem, September 29\nStockholm, September 30\nChicago, September 30\nSingapore, October 1\nEspoo (Helsinki), October 1\nDallas, October 13\nTokyo, October 15\nSydney, October 20\nParis, November 19\nNew Delhi, November 20\nUNLOCK 2026 is complimentary for customers, prospective customers, and partners. To register for a city near you, visit saviynt.com/unlock-roadshow.\nNoYesArtificial Intelligence03 Sep, 2026",
    "hasSummary": true,
    "link": "https://financialit.net/news/artificial-intelligence/saviynt-brings-ai-identity-security-global-stage-unlock-2026-roadshow",
    "source": "Financial IT",
    "tags": [
      "Saviynt",
      "Amazon Web Services"
    ],
    "origin": "rss",
    "pubDate": "2026-09-03T08:23:09.000Z",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-03T09:01:07.104Z",
    "isDuplicateOf": null,
    "content": "Saviynt has announced its global UNLOCK 2026 Roadshow, a 12-city event series focusing on AI identity security. Sponsored globally by Amazon Web Services, the roadshow will explore strategies for securing human, non-human, and AI identities using Saviynt's platforms. The tour begins in September 2026 and will visit major international cities, offering keynotes, live demonstrations, and networking opportunities for security executives and industry experts.",
    "slug": "saviynt-brings-ai-identity-security-to-global-stage-with-unlock-2026-roadshow"
